n, in polar coordinates, is given by \n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{{e}^{r}}{r}.\n$$\n\nNext, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{e}^{r}}{r}\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{e}^{r}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={e}^{r}{|}_{1}^{3}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =({e}^{3}-e)\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =2\\pi ({e}^{3}-e)\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{e}^{r}}{r}\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{r}^{2}{e}^{r}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =({r}^{2}-2r+2){e}^{r}{|}_{1}^{3}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =(5{e}^{3}-e)\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =2\\pi (5{e}^{3}-e)\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $2\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =2\\pi (5{e}^{3}-e)+{2}^{2}\\cdot 2\\pi ({e}^{3}-e) \\\\  & =2\\pi (9{e}^{3}-5e)\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371011 13194139535862 true] [17592186371010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371012 13194139535862 true] [17592186371010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371013 13194139535862 true] [17592186371010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371014 13194139535862 true] [17592186371010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371015 13194139535862 true] [17592186371010 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535862 true] [17592186371010 1041 "selection" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371010 1104