dot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nIf the moment of inertia of the same lamina about another perpendicular line is $7\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ find the distance between the two lines." 13194139535862 true] [17592186371051 1113 #uuid "39a8451a-e3d3-5731-af49-8935d7153d2c" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371051 1145 "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nApplying the parallel axis theorem and solving for $d,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\ 7 & =4+6{d}^{2} \\\\ 6{d}^{2} & =3 \\\\ {d}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ d & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance between the two axes is $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,m.$" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371052 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371053 13194139535862 true] [17592186371052 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371054 13194139535862 true] [17592186371052 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371055 13194139535862 true] [17592186371052 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371056 13194139535862 true] [17592186371052 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371057 13194139535862 true] [17592186371052 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535862 true] [17592186371052 1041 "selection" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371052 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371054 13194139535862 true] [17592186371052 1110 #uuid "ba48e99b-ff5d-5759-a3b9-6cce867b11fc" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371053 1034 "2\\,m" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371053 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535862 true] [17592186371053 1111 #uuid "7447dc25-8ae7-5746-a7c2-2a0dabedcb67" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371054 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,m" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371054 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 131