}^{2} & =\\frac{15}{4} \\\\ {d}^{2} & =\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ d & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance between the two axes is $\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\,m.$" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371059 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371060 13194139535862 true] [17592186371059 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371061 13194139535862 true] [17592186371059 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371062 13194139535862 true] [17592186371059 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371063 13194139535862 true] [17592186371059 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371064 13194139535862 true] [17592186371059 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535862 true] [17592186371059 1041 "selection" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371059 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371063 13194139535862 true] [17592186371059 1110 #uuid "4d108581-aed1-5e62-8db5-99c95c1c2e27" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371060 1034 "\\frac{5}{4}\\,m" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371060 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535862 true] [17592186371060 1111 #uuid "abc54ca4-99a2-594a-9089-7675437dda99" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371061 1034 "\\sqrt{2}\\,m" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371061 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535862 true] [17592186371061 1111 #uuid "f7fecd53-fcab-588c-abeb-ec8178516014" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371062 1034 "4\\,m" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371062 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535862 true] [17592186371062 1111 #uuid "139d3597-f54b-5789-bb5d-1e85bca114a0" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371063 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\,m" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371063 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535862 true] [17592186371063 1111 #uuid "2ad807ef-5374-540e-ab78-17c02b660e3d" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371064 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\,m" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371064 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535862 true] [17592186371064 1111 #uuid "70e148ec-35da-5a90-a0ff-e675d7ae7bbb" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371065 1017 #edb/ref 17592186371066 13194139535862 true] [17592186371065 1089 "q-164132" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371065 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535862 true] [17592186371065 1100 "A circular plate of mass $3\\,\\text{kg}$ with uniform mass density occupies the region of a disk $D$ of radius $2\\,\\text{m}$ and is centered at the origin.\nGiven that the moment of inertia of the plate about a line $l$ perpendicular to the plate is $15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ find the distance of the line $l$ from the center of mass of $D.$" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371065 1113 #uuid "5b1269dc-9a9c-5e0c-a19a-b98eb7ba6d4e" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371065 1145 "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe area of the circular plate $D$ is $A=\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}=4\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{3}{4\\pi }\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid $(0,0).$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{2}\\cdot \\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4\\pi }\\cdot 4\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally