 mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{3}\\cdot y{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =9\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass $(2,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}((x-\\overset{¯}{x})^{2}+(y-\\overset{¯}{y})^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}((x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}((x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2})2x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2x(x-2)^{2}+2x(y-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[2x(x-2)^{2}y+\\frac{2}{3}x(y-1)^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}4x(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{4}{3}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}4{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}+16x+\\frac{4}{3}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}4{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}+\\frac{52}{3}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{4}-\\frac{16}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{26}{3}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =81-144+78-0 \\\\  & =15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =15+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})}^{2}\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =15+4 \\\\  & =19\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371094 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371095 13194139535862 true] [17592186371094 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371096 13194139535862 true] [17592186371094 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371097 13194139535862 true] [17592186371094 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371098 13194139535862 true] [17592186371094 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371099 13194139535862 true] [17592186371094 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535862 true] [175921863