text{m}}^{2},$ about a line perpendicular to the disk passing through a point on the circumference." 13194139535862 true] [17592186371114 1113 #uuid "2b73e87d-4517-5d33-b6a8-a5f0a1bd251a" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371114 1145 "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nSince the mass density is symmetric in $x$ and $y,$ its center of mass is at $(0,0).$ The mass density function, in polar coordinates, is given by $\\lambda (r,\\theta )={r}^{2}.$\n\nNext, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{2}\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =2\\pi \\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{2}\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line passing through a point on the circumference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}+{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}+4\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{20\\pi }{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371115 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371116 13194139535862 true] [17592186371115 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371117 13194139535862 true] [17592186371115 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371118 13194139535862 true] [17592186371115 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371119 13194139535862 true] [17592186371115 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371120 13194139535862 true] [17592186371115 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535862 true] [17592186371115 1041 "selection" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371115 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371118 13194139535862 true] [17592186371115 1110 #uuid "9f74e85b-0d83-5528-b6d3-e84f09bb1db7" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371116 1034 "\\frac{11\\pi }{2}" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371116 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535862 true] [17592186371116 1111 #uuid "38315fe3-f714-57e6-bf09-d988b60d413c" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371117 1034 "8\\pi " 13194139535862 true] [17592186371117 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535862 true] [17592186371117 1111 #uuid "38d7f0e4-01b0-5718-95f8-006d835cd658" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371118 1034 "\\frac{20\\pi }{3}" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371118 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535862 true] [17592186371118 1111 #uuid "3a6ef0eb-0346-5387-b6ac-0fe054c21f56" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371119 1034 "6\\pi " 13194139535862 true] [17592186371119 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535862 true] [17592186371119 1111 #uuid "9b0e57e7-152d-5031-a1cb-c821e22e8abc" 13194139535862 true] [17592186371120 1034 "\\frac{17\\pi }{6}" 13194139535862 true] [1759